From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: lpass-va-macro: fail runtime resume when the registers are not restored

va_macro_runtime_resume() ignored the result of regcache_sync() and
reported an active macro with all its clocks enabled although the DMIC and
decimator configuration had not been written back: recording then fails
while the LPASS votes stay held (2026-10-02 GPT-6.1-Sol audit, F7). On
failure, go back to cache-only mode with the whole cache dirty, release the
clocks in reverse order and return the error.

Upstream fixed the same in eb667d0fbdd3 ("ASoC: codecs: lpass-va-macro:
Switch to PM clock framework for runtime PM", linux-next, 7.3 cycle), as
part of a conversion that does not apply here; this is the minimal
equivalent on the 7.2 clock handling (0083).

Hardware (RAM trial with audio): microphone capture after the macro has
runtime-suspended (idle a few seconds, then record) works as before.

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
index f76bf963c..8b69178c4 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
@@ -1770,7 +1770,20 @@ static int va_macro_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 	}
 
 	regcache_cache_only(va->regmap, false);
-	regcache_sync(va->regmap);
+	ret = regcache_sync(va->regmap);
+	if (ret) {
+		/*
+		 * The registers are not what the cache says: stay in cache-only
+		 * mode with the whole cache dirty for the next resume, and do
+		 * not report an active macro holding its clocks.
+		 */
+		dev_err(va->dev, "failed to restore registers: %d\n", ret);
+		regcache_cache_only(va->regmap, true);
+		regcache_mark_dirty(va->regmap);
+		if (va->has_npl_clk)
+			clk_disable_unprepare(va->npl);
+		goto err_npl;
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 
